      "reasoning": "I have the IDs now:\n`Minotaur Skullcleaver` is `p3`.\n`Falkenrath Noble` is `p34`.\nMy blocker `Tithebearer Giant` is `p16`.\n\n`Falkenrath Noble` has Flying. `Tithebearer Giant` cannot block it.\n`Minotaur Skullcleaver` is forcing me to block. If I don't, I take 2 and go to 3. If I do, I take 1 drain and go to 4.\nThe block is mandatory for survival here? No, 3 life vs 4 life.\nBut killing the creature is valuable. If `Skullcleaver` stays, it hits me again next turn.\nSo I block `p3` with `p16`.\n\nMy `Tithebearer Giant` is 4/5. `Skullcleaver` is 2/2. `Giant` survives. `Skullcleaver` dies.\nOutcome:\n- `Skullcleaver` dies.\n- `Noble` triggers: I lose 1, they gain 1.\n- `Independent` from `Noble` hitting me for 2 damage.\n\nWait, `Noble` is attacking too.\n`Noble` is 2/2. It hits me for 2.\nSo I take 2 combat damage + 1 drain = 3 damage total.\nLife: 5 -> 2.\n\nIf I *don't* block `Skullcleaver`:\n- `Skullcleaver` hits for 2.\n- `Noble` hits for 2.\n- Total 4 damage.\nLife: 5 -> 1.\n\nBlocking saves me 1 life and kills a creature.\nThis is strictly better.\n\nWait, do they have a trick? They have 1 card in hand.\nLands:\n`Mountain` (tapped: p4, p40)\n`Swamp` (tapped: p8, p9, p31)\n`Swamp` (untapped: p45)\nThey have 1 black mana open.\nPossible tricks for {B}:\n- `Supernatural Stamina` (gives +2/+0 and returns to battlefield? No, usually +2/+0 and tapped). If +2/+0, `Skullcleaver` becomes 4/2. Trades with `Giant`.\n- `Unexpected Fangs` (+1/+1 counter)? `Skullcleaver` becomes 3/3. `Giant` is 4/5. `Giant` wins.\n- `Village Rites` (sac)?\n- `Bone Splinters` (sorcery speed)?\n- `Tragic Slip` (-1/-1 or -13/-13)?\n\nIf they have a trick that pumps power to 5, my `Giant` dies.\nExamples: `Titanic Growth` (G, not B), `Brute Force` (R, tapped out of red).\nSo with only {B} open, combat tricks are limited.\nMost likely safe block.\n\nI will block `p3` with `p16`.\n\nOne more thing: `Lightning Visionary` is present (3/2 prowess). It is sick.\nSo my `Giant` is my only defense against their 2 attackers.\nWait, `Tithebearer Giant` is my only creature? Yes.\nAnd `Noble` has flying, so I can only block `Skullcleaver`.\n\nThe plan is settled.\n\nBlockers: `p16:p3` (Giant blocks Skullcleaver).\n\nAlso, I should chat. It's been a while. The situation is dire but exciting. \"Giant block!\" seems appropriate.\n\nWait, actually, I should double check the `Minotaur Skullcleaver` ability.\n\"When {this} enters, it gets +2/+0 until end of turn.\"\nDoes it have that buff NOW?\nIt entered previously? No, it looks like it's been on board.\nWait, let's look at Turn 6 recap.\n\"Combat: Minotaur Skullcleaver -> Gem3P ESPN\".\nIt attacked last turn? Yes.\nSo it lost the +2/+0 buffer. It is a 2/2 now.\nGame state confirms: `power: 2, toughness: 2`.\nThe text \"When {this} enters...\" is just oracle text. It doesn't mean it just entered.\nSafe.\n\nFinal decision: Block `p3` with `p16`.\n\nOne minor detail: `Oathsworn Vampire` in their graveyard.\nMy `Oathsworn Vampire` died.\nWhy is it in *their* graveyard?\nAh, maybe they played `Reanimate` on *my* `Oathsworn Vampire`?\nGame state for me: `gy=[Crypt Lurker, Reanimate]`.\nGame state for them: `gy=[..., Oathsworn Vampire, ...]`.\nWait. My `Oathsworn Vampire` died attacking last turn. It should be in MY graveyard.\nWhy is it not in mine?\nMaybe `Falkenrath Noble` or something exiled it? No.\nMaybe I misread the `get_game_state` output?\n`Gem3P ESPN` graveyard:\n- `Crypt Lurker`\n- `Reanimate`\nStart of Turn 6 battlefield had `Oathsworn Vampire`.\nI attacked with `Crypt Lurker` and `Oathsworn Vampire`?\nNo, I attacked with `Crypt Lurker` only in Turn 6.\nWait, did `Oathsworn Vampire` die?\nThe previous turn log says: `Combat: Crypt Lurker -> Gem3F Proud`.\nIt doesn't mention `Oathsworn Vampire` attacking.\nBut the board state in Turn 7 shows `Oathsworn Vampire` is GONE from my board.\nDid they kill it in their turn?\n\"Stack: [Falkenrath Noble]\"... wait, `Mugging` is in their yard.\nMaybe they