      "reasoning": "My turn. It's Turn 7. (Game state says `Turn 7 COMBAT` just ended, so this must be Turn 8 PRECOMBAT_MAIN? No, the game log says \"Turn 7 PRECOMBAT_MAIN - Gem3P ESPN\". Wait. The previous turn was my turn, Turn 6. My opponent must have just had Turn 7. So this is... Turn 8? Or did I miss a turn?\nLet's check `get_game_state` turn number if needed. But let's look at the board.\nI am at 2 HP. Opponent at 20 HP.\nMy board: `Tithebearer Giant` (4/5).\nTheir board: `Falkenrath Noble` (2/2, tapped, Flying), `Lightning Visionary` (2/1, sick).\nThey have 1 card in hand.\nIn their graveyard: `Mugging`, `Oathsworn Vampire`, `Sure Strike`, `Minotaur Skullcleaver`.\nNote: `Oathsworn Vampire` is in their yard. Did they reanimate it and it died again? Or did I misread ownership? It doesn't matter much unless I try to interact with it.\n\nI drew `Goremand` (6 mana 5/5 Flying Trample, Sac cost).\nI have 6 lands untapped! (4 Plains, 1 Swamp, 1 Thriving Heath (B)). Total 6 mana.\nI can cast `Goremand`.\nCost: {4}{B}{B}. I have 2 Black sources?\nLands:\n`Plains` (W)\n`Plains` (W)\n`Plains` (W)\n`Plains` (W)\n`Swamp` (B)\n`Thriving Heath` (chosen Black) -> (B)\nYes, I have exactly 2 Black mana.\nSo I can cast `Goremand`.\nAdditional cost: Sacrifice a creature.\nI have `Tithebearer Giant`.\nIf I sac `Tithebearer Giant`:\n- `Goremand` enters.\n- Enters triggers: Each opponent sacrifices a creature.\n- They have `Falkenrath Noble` and `Lightning Visionary`.\n- They will likely sac `Lightning Visionary` (2/1) to keep the `Noble` (drain engine).\n- If they sac a creature, `Noble` triggers. I lose 1 life, they gain 1.\n- I am at 2 life. Losing 1 puts me to 1 life.\n- Then I have a 5/5 Flying Trample against their 2/2 Flying.\n- `Goremand` is a Demon.\n- Wait, I have `Archfiend's Vessel` in hand.\n- \"When {this} enters, if it entered from your graveyard... create a 5/5 Demon.\"\n- Not relevant for `Goremand`.\n\nWait, if I cast `Goremand`, I go to 1 life.\nNext turn they untap.\nThey have `Falkenrath Noble`.\nIf they play a removal spell on `Goremand`: `Noble` triggers -> I die.\nIf they just attack with `Falkenrath Noble` (Flying):\n- `Goremand` has Flying. I can block.\n- 5/5 vs 2/2. `Noble` dies.\n- `Noble` triggers on its own death? \"Whenever {this} or another creature dies...\". Yes.\n- So if I block `Noble` and kill it, I lose 1 life.\n- I am at 1 life. I die.\n\nSo...\nScenario 1: Cast `Goremand`.\n- Sac `Giant`. `Noble` triggers. I go to 1 life.\n- They sac `Visionary`. `Noble` triggers. I go to 0 life.\n- I LOSE THE GAME.\n\nCRITICAL: `Falkenrath Noble` triggers WHENEVER a creature dies.\nAny creature. Mine or theirs.\nIf I sac `Giant` to cast `Goremand`, `Giant` dies.\n`Noble` triggers: I lose 1 life.\nThen `Goremand` enters.\nOpponent sacs a creature.\n`Noble` triggers: I lose 1 life.\nI am at 2 life.\n2 - 1 - 1 = 0.\nI die immediately upon resolving `Goremand`.\n\nOkay, `Goremand` is SUICIDE. DO NOT CAST GOREMAND.\n\nAlternatives:\n`Mire Triton` (2/1 Deathtouch, gain 2 life). {1}{B}.\nThis gains me 2 life!\nI go to 4 life.\nAlso mills 2 cards.\nPossible mill hits: `Archfiend's Vessel`? No, I have one in hand. Other reanimation targets?\nI have `Reanimate` in graveyard.\nWait... `Reanimate` costs life equal to casting cost. That's risky.\n\n`Archfiend's Vessel` (1/1 Lifelink). {B}.\nLifelink is good.\nIf I can block with it, I gain life? No, it's 1/1.\n\n`Valorous Stance` {1}{W}. Destroys toughness 4 or greater, or Indestructible.\n`Noble` is 2/2. `Visionary` is 2/1. No targets for destroy.\nCan use for Indestructible to save a creature.\n\n`Divine Verdict` {3}{W}. Destroy attacking/blocking creature.\nGood for defense.\n\nStrategy:\nI need to maximize life and board presence without dying to `Noble` triggers.\n1. Cast `Mire Triton`.\n- Gain 2 life. (Life: 2 -> 4).\n- Mill 2.\n- I have a 2/1 Deathtouch blocker.\n2. Cast `Archfiend's Vessel`.\n- 1/1 Lifelink blocker.\n3. Hold up `Divine Verdict` or `Valorous Stance`.\nI have 6 mana.\n`Mire Triton` (2) + `Archfiend's Vessel` (1) = 3 mana.\nLeft with 3 mana.\n`Divine Verdict` costs 4. I can't hold it up if I cast both creatures.\nIf I cast `Mire Triton` (2), I have 4 mana left. Perfect for `Divine Verdict`.\nIf `Noble` attacks next turn, I can `Divine Verdict` it.\nTriggers: `Noble` dies -> I lose 1 life. (Life: 4 -> 3).\nThis is survivable.\nAnd `Mire Triton` can trade with `Visionary` on ground.\n\nWait, do I need to attack?\nI have `Tithebearer Giant` (4/5).\nThey have `Noble` (2/2 flying) and `Visionary` (2/1).\nIf I attack with `Giant`:\n- They block with `Visionary`? `Visionary` (2/1) chumps `Giant` (4/5).\n- `Visionary` dies. `Noble` triggers. I lose 1 life.\n- If I'm at 4 (after Triton), I go to 3.\n- If they don't block, they take 4. (Life: 20 -> 16).\nApplying pressure is good, but my life total is critical.\nHowever, if I don't attack, `Giant` stays back. `Giant` can't block `Noble` (flying).\n`Giant` can block `Visionary`.\nIf I attack, `Giant` is tapped. `Visionary` attacks me for 2 (or 3 with prowess).\nIf I'm at 4, taking 2 is okay. Taking 3 is okay (go to 1).\nBut `Noble` attacks for 2 flying.\nIf I attack, I have no air defense (unless I draw removal or reach).\nWait, I have `Divine Verdict` in hand!\nSo if I keep 4 mana open:\n- I cast `Mire Triton`. Gain 2 life -> 4.\n- `Giant` stays back? Or attacks?\n- If `Giant` attacks and taps:\n- Their turn: `Noble` attacks (2 dmg). `Visionary` attacks (2 dmg).\n- If I don't block `Visionary`: I take 2+2=4. I die (at exactly 4 life).\n- If I use `Divine Verdict` on `Noble`:\n- `Noble` dies. Trigger (-1 life, total 3).\n- `Visionary` hits for 2. (Life 1).\n- I survive with 1 life.\n- BUT `Divine Verdict` costs {3}{W}. `Mire Triton` costs {1}{B}.\n- Total mana needed: 2 + 4 = 6.\n- I have exactly 6 mana.\n- Colors: {1}{B} + {3}{W} = {4}{W}{B}.\n- I have 2 Black sources? Yes (`Swamp`, `Thriving Heath` black).\n- I have 4 White sources? Yes (`Plains` x4).\n- So I CAN cast `Mire Triton` AND hold up `Divine Verdict`.\n\nThis seems like the best play:\n1. Cast `Mire Triton` to gain life buffer (up to 4).\n2. Pass turn.\n3. Hold priority for `Divine Verdict` on their turn to kill `Falkenrath Noble` or whatever attacks.\n4. Block `Visionary` with `Tithebearer Giant` if they attack on ground. Or `Mire Triton`.\nActually `Tithebearer Giant` can block `Visionary` easily (4/5 vs 2/1). `Visionary` dies. `Noble` trigger (-1 life).\nSo if I kill `Noble` with `Verdict`, I take -1 life.\nIf I block `Visionary` and kill it, I take -1 life.\nStarting at 4:\n- Kill `Noble` (-1 -> 3).\n- Block `Visionary` (-1 -> 2).\nI survive with 2 life.\nWait, if I `Verdict` `Noble` *before* damage, I take no combat damage from it.\nCorrect.\nSo:\nTurn 8 (Theirs):\n- Combat.\n- Attack with `Noble` and `Visionary`.\n- I cast `Verdict` on `Noble`.\n- `Noble` dies. Trigger: I lose 1 (Life 4 -> 3).\n- `Visionary` is blocked by `Giant`.\n- `Visionary` dies. `Noble` is already dead. Does `Noble` see `Visionary` die?\n- IF `Noble` is dead, it is not on battlefield to see `Visionary` die.\n- TIMING IS KEY.\n- If I `Verdict` in Declare Attackers or Declare Blockers step:\n- `Noble` dies FIRST. Trigger happens (-1 life).\n- Then combat damage happens (none from `Noble`, `Visionary` blocked).\n- Then `Visionary` dies (damage step).\n- Since `Noble` is gone, NO trigger from `Visionary` death.\n- So I only lose 1 life total.\n- I end up at 3 life.\nThis looks solid.\n\nWhat about `Archfiend's Vessel`?\nIf I cast it (1 mana), I only have 5 mana left.\n`Divine Verdict` needs 4.\nI have 6 total.\nSo 6 - 1 = 5. I can still cast `Verdict`!\nWait.\n`Mire Triton` = 2 mana.\n`Archfiend's Vessel` = 1 mana.\n`Divine Verdict` = 4 mana.\nTotal needed for ALL: 2 + 1 + 4 = 7.\nI have 6.\nSo I choose: `Mire Triton` + `Verdict` OR `Archfiend's Vessel` + `Verdict`.\n`Mire Triton` gains 2 life immediately.\n`Archfiend's Vessel` is 1/1 lifelink. Doesn't gain life immediately.\nSo `Mire Triton` is strictly better for survival range.\n\nSo Plan:\n1. Play `Mire Triton`.\n2. Do NOT play `Archfiend's Vessel`.\n3. Do NOT attack with `Tithebearer Giant` (keep as blocker for `Visionary`).\n4. Pass turn.\n5. React with `Divine Verdict`.\n\nLet's execute step 1: `Mire Triton`.\n\nChat: \"Staying alive! Staying alive! Ah ah ah ah staying alive!\"\n\n",
