      "reasoning": "`Mire Triton` resolved. I milled two `Swamp`s (lucky, no spells lost). Life is 4.\nI have 4 `Plains` untapped.\nI am holding `Divine Verdict` {3}{W} (Wait, `Divine Verdict` costs {3}{W}. I have 4 `Plains` untapped, so {W}{W}{W}{W}. Yes, I can cast it.)\nMy plan is to hold up `Divine Verdict`.\nI have `Valorous Stance` too.\nI will pass the turn and wait for their attack.\n\nDo not attack with `Tithebearer Giant`. `Visionary` (2/1) is sick, so can't attack anyway?\nWait, `Lightning Visionary` is listed as `sick`.\nIf it's sick, it can't attack next turn? (Unless it has haste, which it doesn't).\nWait, earlier I said \"Visionary attacks me for 2\".\nIf `Visionary` is sick NOW (Turn 7 Main), it was just cast?\nLooking at previous turn state: `Turn 7 COMBAT... bf=[... Lightning Visionary 3/2 (sick) ...]`.\nWait, they cast it in their main phase Turn 7?\nYes.\nThen it will NOT be sick on their NEXT turn (Turn 8).\nSo next turn they attack with `Noble` and `Visionary`.\nPlan holds: `Divine Verdict` on `Noble`, Block `Visionary` with `Giant`. (Or block with `Mire Triton` if I want to trade deathtouch? No, `Giant` eats `Visionary` for free).\nWait, `Visionary` has Prowess.\nIf they cast a spell, `Visionary` becomes 3/2 or bigger.\nIf `Giant` blocks (4/5), `Visionary` needs +3 power to trade. That's 3 spells. Unlikely with 1 card in hand.\nBut if they use removal on `Giant`? `Mugging` is sorcery speed. `Sure Strike` is instant.\nIf they have `Sure Strike` (+3/+0 First Strike), `Visionary` becomes 6/2 First Strike?\n3/2 base + 3 = 6.\nBefore damage: `Visionary` 6/2 First Strike deals 6 to `Giant`. `Giant` dies.\n`Giant` never hits back.\nSo `Giant` dies for free.\nBut I have `Divine Verdict`.\nI can Verdict the `Visionary` instead?\nIf `Noble` attacks (flying, 2 dmg). `Visionary` attacks (ground, 2 dmg).\nIf I block `Visionary`. They cast `Sure Strike`.\nI cast `Divine Verdict` on `Visionary`.\n`Visionary` dies. `Sure Strike` fizzles.\n`Noble` hits me for 2. Trigger from `Visionary` death (-1 life).\nResult: I take 2 + 1 = 3 dmg.\nStart 4 -> 1 life. Surviving.\n\nWhat if I `Verdict` the `Noble`?\n`Noble` dies. Trigger (-1 life).\n`Visionary` is blocked by `Giant`.\nThey cast `Sure Strike`. `Visionary` kills `Giant`. `Giant` dies.\n`Giant` trigger (-1 life)? No, `Giant` trigger is on enter. But `Giant` dying triggers... nothing.\nWait, `Noble` is dead. Does `Noble` see `Giant` die?\nIf `Noble` dies in declare blockers step, it is gone before damage step.\nSo `Noble` does NOT see `Giant` die.\nSo I take -1 from `Noble` death.\nZero from `Noble` combat.\nZero from `Visionary` combat (blocked).\nMy `Giant` dies.\nI end up at 3 life.\nBut I lose my 4/5.\n\nWhich is better?\nA) `Verdict` `Visionary` in response to trick. Keep `Giant`. Take `Noble` hit. (1 life left).\nB) `Verdict` `Noble`. Lose `Giant`. Take no combat damage. (3 life left).\n3 life is safer than 1.\nBut keeping a 4/5 is huge.\nAlso they only have 1 card. If it's NOT pump, `Giant` eats `Visionary`.\nIf I `Verdict` `Noble`, `Giant` eats `Visionary` safely assuming no trick.\nIf they have a trick, `Giant` might die.\nKilling `Noble` removes the drain effect which is the biggest threat.\nKilling `Noble` is priority.\nSo plan: Hold up `Verdict`. Kill `Noble` if it attacks. Block `Visionary` with `Giant`.\n\nFinal Check:\nPass turn.\n\n",
