      "player": "Gem3P ESPN",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "They attacked with both `Falkenrath Noble` (2/2 Flying) and `Lightning Visionary` (2/1).\nI am at 4 life.\n`Noble` is flying, I cannot block it.\n`Visionary` is ground, I can block it with `Tithebearer Giant` (4/5) or `Mire Triton` (2/1 Deathtouch).\n\nThis is the moment for `Divine Verdict`.\nI need to kill `Falkenrath Noble` to stop the drain trigger and the flying damage.\nWait, if I kill `Noble` NOW (Declare Attackers step), `Noble` dies. Trigger happens.\nI lose 1 life (4 -> 3).\n`Noble` is gone. So no combat damage from `Noble`.\nThe only attacker left is `Lightning Visionary`.\nI can block `Visionary` in the Declare Blockers step (coming up next).\nIf I block `Visionary` with `Giant` (4/5), `Visionary` (2/1) dies. `Giant` lives.\nDoes `Noble` trigger on `Visionary`'s death?\nNO, because `Noble` died in Declare Attackers step. It's not on the battlefield when `Visionary` dies in Combat Damage step.\nSo I take -1 life total from this combat.\nI survive at 3 life.\nThis is optimal.\n\nWait, `Valorous Stance` is also an option.\n\"Destroy target creature with toughness 4 or greater.\"\n`Noble` is 2/2. `Visionary` is 2/1. No targets for destroy.\n\"Target creature gains indestructible.\"\nNot useful for removing attackers.\n\nSo `Divine Verdict` on `Falkenrath Noble` is the play.\nTarget: `Falkenrath Noble` (ID p34 from earlier, check `incoming_attackers` or `bf` if needed, but the tool will give me choices).\nAh, `Divine Verdict` targets \"target attacking or blocking creature\".\nBoth are attacking. I must choose the target.\nChoices will be presented after I select the card.\n\nLet's cast `Divine Verdict` on `Falkenrath Noble`.\n\nWait, verify mana. {3}{W}. I have 4 Plains. Cost is covered.\nI have 4 life.\n`Noble` dies -> 1 drain damage -> 3 life.\n`Visionary` -> Blocked -> 0 damage.\nUnless they have a trick.\nThey have 1 card in hand.\nIf they have `Sure Strike` (+3/+0 First Strike) on `Visionary`.\n`Visionary` becomes 5/1 First Strike.\nIf I block with `Giant` (4/5). `Giant` takes 5 damage and dies before dealing damage.\n`Giant` dies.\nI take no trample damage (Visionary has no trample).\nMy `Giant` dies. I lose a creature.\nIf I block with `Mire Triton` (2/1 Deathtouch).\n`Visionary` (First Strike) hits `Triton`. `Triton` dies.\n`Triton` (Deathtouch) does NOT hit back because `Visionary` has First Strike.\nSo `Mire Triton` dies for free.\nBAD.\n\nSo `Giant` is the safer block against First Strike, but it still dies.\nHowever, I have no choice. I must block `Visionary` to survive.\nIf I don't block `Visionary`, I take 2 damage.\nIf I killed `Noble` (-1 life), took 2 from `Visionary` -> I go to 1 life.\nThis is also survivable (barely).\nAnd I keep my creature.\nBUT `Visionary` has Prowess.\nIf they cast `Sure Strike`, `Visionary` gets +1/+1 (Prowess) +3/+0 (Spell) = +4/+1 total.\nSo `Visionary` becomes 6/2 First Strike.\nIf unblocked: I take 6 damage. I DIE.\nSo I MUST block `Visionary` if there's any chance of Prowess/Pump.\nSo I will block `Visionary` with `Giant` (or `Triton`).\nPrefer blocking with `Giant`? No, if `Giant` blocks and they have trick, `Giant` dies.\nIf `Giant` blocks and NO trick, `Visionary` dies.\nBlocking is correct.\n\nStep 1: Cast `Divine Verdict` on `Falkenrath Noble` NOW.\n\n",
