      "reasoning": "I must block `Lightning Visionary` (2/1).\nBlockers:\n- `Tithebearer Giant` (4/5)\n- `Mire Triton` (2/1, Deathtouch)\n\n`Visionary` has Prowess.\nIf I block with `Giant` (4/5).\nIf they have a trick (e.g. `Sure Strike` +3/+0 First Strike), `Visionary` becomes 6/2 First Strike (2/1 base + 1/1 prowess + 3/0 spell).\n`Visionary` hits `Giant` for 6. `Giant` dies.\n`Giant` hits nothing (First Strike).\nI lose `Giant`.\n\nIf I block with `Mire Triton` (2/1).\n`Visionary` becomes 6/2 First Strike.\n`Triton` dies.\n`Triton` hits nothing.\nI lose `Triton`.\n\nIf they have NO trick:\n`Giant` (4/5) blocks `Visionary` (2/1). `Visionary` deals 2 to `Giant` (survives). `Giant` deals 4 to `Visionary` (dies).\nI keep `Giant` (damage marked 2).\n`Triton` (2/1) blocks `Visionary` (2/1). They trade. Both die.\nI lose `Triton`.\n\nConclusion: Blocking with `Giant` is strictly better IF they have no trick.\nIf they DO have a trick, I lose a creature either way.\nLosing `Giant` (4/5) is worse than losing `Triton` (2/1).\nWait, if I lose `Giant`, I have `Goremand` fodder?\nNo, `Goremand` needs me to stick a creature.\nIf I block with `Triton` and it dies, I have `Giant` left. `Giant` is 4/5. Usually better than `Triton`.\nSo risking `Giant` seems bad if I expect a trick.\nBut `Triton` is expendable. `Giant` is a beater/wall.\nAlso `Mire Triton` gains me 2 life on ETB, which I already got. It's done its job.\nIts deathtouch is valuable against big things, but `Visionary` is small.\n\nHowever, if they have `Sure Strike`, do they use it on `Visionary` if blocked by `Triton`?\nYes, to kill `Triton` without trading.\nIf blocked by `Giant`, they use it to kill `Giant` (a huge threat).\nThey would definitely favor killing `Giant`.\nSo if I block with `Giant`, they use the trick.\nIf I block with `Triton`, they might use the trick or just trade?\nNo, `Sure Strike` saves `Visionary` from trading. `Visionary` lives.\nSo they use it either way.\nSo do I want to lose `Giant` or `Triton`?\n`Giant` is 4/5. `Triton` is 2/1.\n`Giant` is better.\nSo I should protect `Giant`.\nWait... if I block with `Triton` and they have `Sure Strike`, `Triton` dies and `Visionary` lives.\nMy board: `Giant`. Their board: `Visionary`. Hand: 0 cards.\nIf I block with `Giant` and they have `Sure Strike`, `Giant` dies and `Visionary` lives.\nMy board: `Triton`. Their board: `Visionary`. Hand: 0 cards.\nClearly I prefer having `Giant` on board.\n\nSo blocking with `Mire Triton` is the safer play to protect my best creature (`Giant`).\nBUT, if they *don't* have a trick (which is possible, last card could be land or irrelevant),\nBlock with `Giant`: `Visionary` dies. `Giant` lives. I have `Giant` + `Triton`. Best outcome.\nBlock with `Triton`: `Visionary` dies (trade). `Triton` dies. I have `Giant`. Good outcome.\nThe upside of blocking with `Giant` is keeping both creatures.\nThe downside is losing `Giant` to a potential trick.\nThe downside of blocking with `Triton` (if no trick) is losing `Triton` needlessly.\n\nProbabilities:\nThey have 1 card.\nThey had 26 cards in library.\nIs it `Sure Strike`?\nThe graveyard shows `Sure Strike` x1.\nIs there another?\nCommon deck construction rules (draft/sealed): could be multiples.\nThere is a risk.\nBut `Giant` eating `Visionary` is such a good value.\nAnd 4/5 blocks 2/x all day.\nI'm at 3 life. I need board presence.\nI'll risk the `Giant` block. It maximizes upside (keeping both creatures).\nIf `Giant` dies, I still have `Triton` (which can block `Visionary` next time potentially, or trade).\nWait. If `Giant` dies, I have `Triton`.\nIf `Triton` dies, I have `Giant`.\n`Giant` is better.\nSo losing `Giant` is worse.\nBut only *if* they have the card.\nIf they don't, I keep `Giant` AND `Triton`.\nVs keeping `Giant` only.\nDifference = 1 creature (`Triton`).\nThe value of keeping `Triton` (a 2/1) is decent.\nBut is it worth the risk of losing `Giant`?\nIf `Giant` dies, I am left with a 2/1 vs their... whatever.\nIf `Triton` dies, I am left with a 4/5.\n4/5 dominates the board (except `Noble` flying, but `Noble` is dead).\n`Visionary` is 2/1.\nSo preserving `Giant` guarantees I have a 4/5.\nPreserving `Triton` guarantees... nothing much.\nSo I should ensure `Giant` survives.\nSo I should block with...\nWait.\nScenario A (Block w/ Giant):\n- No Trick: `Visionary` dies. `Giant` lives. (Result: I have 4/5 + 2/1).\n- Trick: `Giant` dies. `Visionary` lives. (Result: I have 2/1).\n\nScenario B (Block w/ Triton):\n- No Trick: `Visionary` dies. `Triton` dies. (Result: I have 4/5).\n- Trick: `Triton` dies. `Visionary` lives. (Result: I have 4/5).\n\nReview:\nSafest floor is Scenario B (I always have 4/5).\nHighest ceiling is Scenario A (I have 4/5 + 2/1).\nLowest floor is Scenario A (I have 2/1).\nIs the 2/1 worth risking the 4/5?\nNo. `Triton` is a 2/1. `Giant` is the win condition.\nIf I'm left with only `Mire Triton`, I'm in trouble.\nSo I should take the safe route: Block with `Mire Triton`.\nActually I can block with BOTH?\nIf I block with `Giant` AND `Triton`.\nThey order blockers.\nIf they have a trick (`Sure Strike`):\n`Visionary` 6/2 First Strike.\nThey assign 2 damage to first blocker, 4 to second?\nNo, 6 damage to first blocker.\nIf they order `Giant` first: `Giant` dies. `Triton` untouched?\nWait. `Visionary` deals combat damage.\nFirst Strike damage step: `Visionary` deals 6.\nTo `Giant` (4/5)? It deals all 6 to kill it. Or 5 to kill it, 1 to `Triton`.\n`Giant` dies. `Triton` maybe dies.\nBad.\nDouble blocking doesn't help against First Strike + High Power.\n\nSo single block with `Mire Triton` is the \"safe\" play to ensure `Giant` survives.\n`Giant` is crucial.\nI will block with `Mire Triton`. `p50`.\nAttacker is `Lightning Visionary` (p36? Check previous log or infer).\nWait, I need attacker ID.\nGame state says: `Combat: -> Gem3P ESPN | Lightning Visionary -> Gem3P ESPN`.\nEarlier log showed `Lightning Visionary` ID is `p36` (implied from choices, or I can guess).\nPrompt: \"Respo