      "reasoning": "`Valorous Stance` (Destroy mode) is on the stack targeting `Rodolf`.\nThey have no cards.\n(Wait, \"hand=1 lib=26\" from Turn 8 PRECOMBAT_MAIN decision initially? No, that was before. Last decision said \"hand=0\". Yes, prompt before showed \"hand=1\". But my previous thought was \"They have 0 cards in hand\". What happened?\nTurn 8 PRECOMBAT_MAIN prompt: `Gem3F Proud: 21hp lib=26 bf=... hand=...`? No, log just says `bf=...` and `gy=...`.\nWait, Turn 8 COMBAT decision (earlier): `Gem3F Proud: 21hp hand=1`.\nTurn 8 PRECOMBAT_MAIN (this turn): Their hand count is not shown in my recap, but `Pass Priority` calls show it.\nLet's check previous `pass_priority`: `Gem3F Proud: 21hp lib=26 bf=... gy=...`. Hand count missing?\nWait. `default_api:tool_pass_priority_cWgtJqrsgWhf0rPyrYfe` output: `Decision ... Gem3F Proud: 21hp lib=26 bf=...`. It does NOT list hand size explicitly?\nAh, usually it says `Gem3F Proud: 21hp hand=X`. If X=0, maybe it omits it?\nOr I missed it.\nAh, previous COMBAT had `hand=1`.\nTurn 8 PRECOMBAT_MAIN (mine): I drew `Skyhunter Patrol`.\nDid they play their card?\nIf they played `Rodolf` last turn (Turn 8), their hand went to 0.\nYes, `Rodolf` is sick. It entered Turn 8 Main (their turn).\nSo now (Turn 8 My Turn - actually Turn 9?), `Rodolf` is sick?\nWait. The turn counter says Turn 8.\nIf it's Turn 8, and I am acting, and they attacked previously...\nWait. Turn numbers increment per player turn usually? Or pairs?\nUsually Turn N is Player 1 Turn N, Player 2 Turn N.\nIf prompt says `Turn 8 PRECOMBAT_MAIN - Gem3P ESPN`. That means it's MY turn 8.\nSo Turn 7 was their turn 7? Or Turn 8 was their turn 8?\nIf `Rodolf` is sick, it entered on MY turn?\nNo, sickness lasts until you control it since the beginning of your turn.\nIf they cast it on THEIR turn, it is sick on their turn.\nOn MY turn, it is no longer sick for them.\nBut the board says `Rodolf Duskbringer 4/4 (sick)`.\nThis implies it entered **on my turn**?\nHow? Did they have Flash? No. `Rodolf` is not Flash.\nDid I cast `Reanimate`? No.\nDid they cast it?\nWait. Maybe the \"sick\" label persists until their next turn begins?\nYes. Summoning sickness wears off at the start of YOUR turn.\nSo during my turn, their creature is still technically \"sick\" (summoning sick), though it doesn't matter for blocking because blocking doesn't require tap (unless tapped).\nAnd it's untapped. So it can block.\nSo `Valorous Stance` is definitely needed to remove it as a blocker anyway?\nWait, if it can block, `Giant` (4/5) would be blocked by `Rodolf` (4/4 Deathtouch Lifelink).\n`Giant` dies. They gain 4 life.\nThis is terrible.\nSo `Valorous Stance` before attacks is CRITICAL.\nCorrect play.\n\nPass priority to resolve `Valorous Stance`.\n\n",
