      "reasoning": "`Rodolf` is dead. The path is clear.\n`Tithebearer Giant` (4/5) can attack for 4.\nI have 4 mana left.\nI can cast `Skyhunter Patrol` (2WW).\nHowever, `Skyhunter Patrol` is not haster, so it can't attack.\nSo I should cast it post-combat?\nNo reason to delay unless I suspect Trickery.\nIf I cast it now (Pre-Combat), they know what I have to block with next turn. (Information disadvantage?)\nIf I attack first, then cast it Second Main, they might think I missed a land drop or have a trick? No, I played a land already? No, land drops remaining: 1. `Untapped lands: 6`.\nWait, I used 2 mana (`Valorous Stance`). I have 4 left.\nIf I play land + `Skyhunter`, I have 0 left.\nIf I don't play land, I have `Skyhunter`.\nActually, does it matter?\nCasting `Skyhunter` gives them information.\nBut if I attack with `Giant`, they take 4.\nThen Second Main -> `Skyhunter`.\nIs there any reason to cast `Skyhunter` *before* combat?\nOnly if it buffs `Giant`? No.\nOnly if it has Haste? No.\nOnly if it triggers Prowess? No Prowess on my side.\nDoes it trigger anything else? `Archfiend's Vessel` in hand... no.\nSo casting Post-Combat is strictly better for information hiding (though trivial since they have no cards).\nAlso, if `Giant` somehow dies (e.g. they have an instant kill spell I forgot about?), I might want to hold mana for `Archfiend's Vessel` or `Goremand` next turn?\nNo, I'm tapping out for `Skyhunter` anyway.\nI will attack first. `Combat Phase`.\n\nPass priority (move to Combat).\n\n",
