      "reasoning": "Turn 10 (My Turn 9).\nI drew `Kami of Ancient Law`.\nMy hand: `Archfiend's Vessel`, `Goremand`, `Kami of Ancient Law`.\nBoard: `Skyhunter Patrol` (2/3 Flying First Strike), `Tithebearer Giant` (4/5), plus 6 lands.\nOpponent: 17 life, 0 creatures, 0 cards in hand (lib=25, bf=8 lands).\nMy plan:\nOption A: Attack with both (2+4 = 6 damage). 11 life left.\nPost-combat: Cast `Goremand` sacrificing `Skyhunter` or `Giant`? Or `Vessel`?\nI can cast `Vessel` ({B}) + `Goremand` ({6}). Total 7 mana.\nI have 6 lands. (4 Plains, 1 Swamp, 1 Heath).\nWait. `Untapped lands: 6`.\nSo I CANNOT cast `Vessel` + `Goremand` this turn.\nIf I cast `Goremand`, I must sac a creature *I control*. (`Skyhunter` or `Giant`).\nIf I sac `Skyhunter`, I lose my flier.\nIf I sac `Giant`, I lose my 4/5. `Goremand` is 5/5 Flying Trample. Upgrade over `Giant` (4/5 ground).\nUpgrade over `Skyhunter` (2/3 flying).\n`Goremand` ETB: Each opponent sacrifices a creature. (They have none).\nSo I'm just upgrading a creature.\nIs it worth it?\n`Goremand` is a threat.\nBut `Skyhunter` and `Giant` are threats too.\nWhy sac one for a slightly bigger one?\nEspecially since they have no board.\nBetter to keep 2 threats than 1 big threat (usually) against spot removal, BUT they have no cards.\nAlso `Goremand` has Trample.\nBut the real play is: Just attack.\nAttack for 6.\nIf I cast `Kami of Ancient Law` ({1}{W}), I have 4 mana left. Not enough for `Goremand`.\nSo I can play `Kami` + `Vessel`.\nThen next turn I can `Goremand` saccing `Vessel`.\nThis seems optimal.\nI widen the board now, enable `Goremand` next turn without losing a \"real\" creature.\nAlso `Kami` is a 2/2.\n\nSo Play: `Kami of Ancient Law` + `Archfiend's Vessel`.\nAttack with `Skyhunter` + `Giant`.\nSequence: Attack first? Or play first?\nIf I play first, no Haste, no Prowess.\nAttack first.\nHide info?\nThey have no cards. Info hiding is minimal value, but correct habit.\nSo Combat -> Attack All -> Post-Combat -> Cast `Kami` + `Vessel`.\n\nWait, `Archfiend's Vessel` cost is {B}.\n`Kami` cost is {1}{W}.\nTotal {1}{W}{B}.\nI have {W}{W}{W}{W}{B}{W/B}.\nPlenty.\n\nLet's go to combat.\n\nAction: `choose_action(choice=\"no\")`.\n\n",
