      "reasoning": "Passed `Kami of Ancient Law`.\nWait, looking at Lands:\n`bf=[Plains (tapped), Plains, Plains, Plains, ..., Swamp (tapped), Thriving Heath (tapped)]`.\nSo 3 Plains untapped.\n`Kami` cost was {1}{W}.\nIt used {1} from `Thriving Heath` (tapped) and {W} from one `Plains`. No?\nWait. `Thriving Heath` produces B (chosen color) or W.\nIf I picked W, it produces W.\nThe other tapped land is a Swamp.\n`Kami` usually costs {1}{W}.\nMaybe it used Heath for {1} (via W or B) and Swamp for {B}? No.\nWhatever.\nI have 3 Plains untapped.\n`Archfiend's Vessel` cost is {B}.\nI need a black source.\nThe Swamp is tapped.\n`Thriving Heath` is tapped.\nUh oh.\nDid I mess up the tapping?\nI had: 4 Plains, 1 Swamp, 1 Heath.\nI cast `Kami` ({1}{W}).\nIt tapped: 1 Plains, 1 Swamp, 1 Heath?\nThat's 3 lands for a 2 mana spell.\nWait. The board says:\n`bf=[Plains (tapped), Plains, Plains, Plains, ... Swamp (tapped), Thriving Heath (tapped)]`.\nSo 3 lands are tapped.\nMaybe I tapped one manually before? No.\nMaybe the system auto-tapped poorly?\nIf I used `auto_tap=true` (default), it picked 3 lands? No, that's impossible.\nOr maybe `Kami` costs {1}{W} and I had 6 lands.\n6 - 2 = 4.\nWhy are 3 untapped?\nAh, because I tapped one manually? No.\nMaybe I miscounted.\nI had 6 lands untapped before `Kami`.\nNow 3.\nSo `Kami` consumed 3 mana?\nOr maybe one was already tapped?\nBefore Combat: `bf=[Plains, Plains, Plains, Plains, Skyhunter, Swamp, Heath, Giant]`.\nAll untapped except creatures? (creatures don't tap for mana).\nSo 6 lands.\nNow 3.\nIs it possible `Kami` cost was increased? No.\nDid I tap `Heath` *twice*?\nI used `choose_action(choice=\"1\")` to select ability 1 of `Heath`.\nMaybe that counted as manual tap? And then auto-tap tapped others?\nThis is a common issue with auto-tap + manual activation.\nIf I manually activate a land, I should include it in `mana_plan` or ensure `auto_tap` accounts for it.\nBut here, I just cast the spell, and the system asked me to clarify