      "reasoning": "My Turn 10?\nHand: `Goremand`, `Ninth Bridge Patrol`.\nBoard: `Vessel`, `Kami`, `Skyhunter`, `Giant`. (4 creatures).\nOpponent: 0 creatures.\nI have 6 lands untapped.\nI need 4B for `Goremand` (Total 6).\nWait, `Goremand` costs {4}{B}{B}. That's 6 mana.\nAdditional cost: Sacrifice a creature.\nIf I cast `Goremand`, I sac `Vessel`?\n`Vessel` says: \"When {this} enters, if it entered from your graveyard... create a 5/5 demon\".\nIf I sac `Vessel` to `Goremand`, it dies.\nIt doesn't enter from graveyard.\nWait.\nIf I have `Vessel` on battlefield. I sac it. It goes to GY.\n`Goremand` enters. Opponent sacs a creature (they have none).\nSo I lose `Vessel` (1/1) and gain `Goremand` (5/5 Flying Trample).\nIs that worth it?\nYes. 5/5 Flyer is huge.\nI can attack first with `Vessel`? No, it has summoning sickness? No, I played it last turn.\nIt is active.\nSo I should attack first!\nAttacking with all:\n`Giant` (4 power)\n`Skyhunter` (2 power, flying)\n`Kami` (2 power)\n`Vessel` (1 power, lifelink)\nTotal: 4+2+2+1 = 9 damage.\nOpponent has 11 life.\nIf they take 9, they go to 2.\nI gain 1 life from `Vessel`.\nThen in Postcombat Main, I cast `Goremand` sacrificing `Vessel` (tapped)?\nYes.\nOr `Kami`?\n`Kami` is 2/2. `Vessel` is 1/1.\nSac `Vessel`.\nThen I have `Goremand` (5/5) + `Giant` + `Skyhunter` + `Kami`.\nOpponent at 2 life facing lethal next turn.\nBUT `Goremand` makes opponent sacrifice a creature. They have none.\nSo that trigger whiffs.\nBut getting a 5/5 Flyer is good.\nIs it better to cast `Ninth Bridge Patrol`?\nBecomes 1/1. Grows when creatures leave.\nIf I cast `Patrol` first, then `Goremand` implies sac. `Patrol` triggers.\n`Patrol` becomes 2/2.\nSo:\n1. Attack first. (Damage 9).\n2. Cast `Ninth Bridge Patrol` ({1}{W}). Leaves 4 mana.\n3. Can't cast `Goremand` ({4}{B}{B} = 6).\nSo I can't do both in one turn unless I have 8 mana. I have 6.\nSo choice is: `Goremand` OR `Patrol` + pass (or just attack).\n`Goremand` is better clock.\nSo sequence:\nAttack with all.\nPostcombat: Cast `Goremand`, sac `Vessel` (or `Kami`).\nSac `Vessel` (1/1) seems best.\nBut `Vessel` has lifelink.\nOpponent at 2 life.\nNext turn they need to deal 3 damage to me.\nIf I have blockers...\n`Giant` and `Kami` will stay back?\nNo, I attack with ALL.\nThey are tapped.\nIf opponent has a haste creature or removal + creature?\nThey have 9 lands.\nIf they cast a big haste threat...\nThey have Black/Red.\nLikely removal.\nIf they remove my blockers, I die?\nWait. I am at 3 life.\nIf I attack with all, I am tapped out.\nIf they drop a 3/3 Haste, I die.\nIs there a 3/3 Haste in M21?\n`Volcanic Geyser` (X spell)? `Shock`?\n`Pitchburn Devils`?\n`Hellkite Punisher`?\nMaybe I should hold back `Kami` or `Giant`?\n`Skyhunter` has Flying, hard to block.\n`Giant` (4/5).\n`Vessel` (1/1 Lifelink).\nIf I attack with `Vessel`, I gain 1 life -> 4 life.\nThat's safer.\nOpponent has no hand (last check), but drew 1 card.\nUnless they sandbagged.\nThey played Mountain last turn.\nSo they have 1 unknown card.\nIt's risky to be tapped out at 3 life vs Red.\nI should keep `Giant` back?\n`Giant` is 4/5. tough blocker.\nIf I attack with `Skyhunter` (2), `Kami` (2), `Vessel` (1).\nTotal 5 damage. Opponent -> 6.\nI gain 1 life -> 4.\nThen Main 2: Cast `Goremand`, sac `Vessel`?\nOr sac `Kami`?\nSac `Vessel` (tapped).\n`Goremand` is 5/5 blocker (Flying).\nSo I will have `Goremand` (untapped) and `Giant` (untapped).\nThat's very safe.\nAnd opponent at 6 life.\nNext turn `Goremand` (5) + `Giant` (4) is lethal.\nWait. `Goremand` flies. 5 damage.\n`Skyhunter` flies. 2 damage.\nTotal 7 flying damage.\nLethal.\nSo I don't need to attack with `Giant` this turn to set up lethal.\nAttacking with `Skyhunter` (2) + `Vessel` (1) + `Kami` (2) puts them to 6.\nNext turn Flying (5+2=7) kills them.\nSo `Giant` can stay back.\nAnd `Kami`?\nIf I sac `Kami` to `Goremand`?\nI have `Vessel` (1/1).\n`Goremand` trigger: Opponent sacs creature. (Whiff).\nIf I sac `Kami` (2/2) instead of `Vessel` (1/1).\nI keep `Vessel` (1/1 lifelink).\n`Vessel` is better to sac because it's smaller?\nBut `Vessel` gains life.\nIf I attack with `Vessel`, it taps.\nI sac it post-combat.\nI gained 1 life (important!).\nSo plan:\nAttack with `Skyhunter`, `Kami`, `Vessel`.\nBlocked? No blockers.\nDamage: 5. Opponent 11 -> 6.\nI gain 1 life -> 4.\nPost-combat: Cast `Goremand`, sac `Vessel`.\nBoard: `Goremand` (5/5 F/T), `Giant` (4/5), `Skyhunter` (2/3 tapped), `Kami` (2/2 tapped).\nOpponent Turn: Facing 4 life, 5/5 blocker, 4/5 blocker.\nMy Turn: Attack with `Goremand` + `Skyhunter` = 7 Flying damage. Lethal.\nStrategy sound.\nAttacking with `Giant` is greedy and risks haste lethal.\nSo: Pass priority to combat.\n\nAction: `choose_action(choice=\"no\")`.\n\n",
