      "betterLine": "Cast Skyhunter Patrol for {2}{W}{W} to add a flying first strike blocker/attacker to the board. At 3 life with no instants in hand, there is no reason to hold mana open.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 269,
      "player": "Gem3P ESPN",
      "decisionIndex": 104
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "At 3 life, passing without casting any creatures is a significant mistake. Archfiend's Vessel (1/1 lifelink for {B}) is critically important as a blocker that gains life, and Kami of Ancient Law (2/2 for {1}{W}) provides another body for blocking. The opponent has no creatures currently but could deploy threats, and having these blockers ready is essential at such low life. There's no strategic reason to hold these cards.",
      "actionTaken": "Passed priority in precombat main without casting any spells",
      "betterLine": "Cast Archfiend's Vessel ({B}) for a lifelink blocker, and Kami of Ancient Law ({1}{W}) for an additional 2/2 blocker. Both are critical at 3 life and cost only 3 mana total, leaving 3 mana open. Could also consider casting Goremand sacrificing Tithebearer Giant for a 5/5 flying trampler.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 294,
      "player": "Gem3P ESPN",
      "decisionIndex": 116
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "At 3 life, the player needs to close the game quickly. Goremand is castable this turn (6 mana available: 4 Plains + Swamp + Thriving Heath for {4}{B}{B}) by sacrificing one of the tapped creatures. A 5/5 flying trample presents a much faster clock than a 2/2 with an irrelevant enchantment-destruction ability (no enchantments in play). Delaying Goremand by a turn at 3 life is dangerous since the opponent could draw removal or threats.",
      "actionTaken": "Cast Kami of Ancient Law, a 2/2 with no relevant ability in this board state.",
